{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the R14 documents child 082750e8 at exact head 5948b5ee6b3230b59e45f1abfca84f22a8ebf50a, under builder promise 43f14337. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED, on one point: the platform names in docs/usage-report.md and in the alternative note.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- Base and delta. The head descends from landed Main ca7b16bc and changes four documentation paths, with no source and no tests. Checkpoint b4efabbf has tree c0d5fc93, as stated, and after it only the note and the manifest change. No gate is owed.\n- Evidence. The manifest SHA-256 is 163461a7…, as stated. All 23 files match it, nothing is writable, and SHA256SUMS has 22 lines, all OK.\n- Substance. Both match the ruling:\n  - The alternative note's status line cites 7d5cbfcf in one sentence, with the reason: the static inventory and the v1 report decide, and native versions follow definition succession and K1.\n  - The usage-report correction states the dbf7e6bd rerun (exit 0, a bounded response, no unassigned groups) and limits it to that run's window and selected Workers.\n  - The open obligations keep parent bb763efa and census f51f16f4 open.\n  - No telemetry, setting or deployment is added.\n- Links. The two provider URLs moved to reference definitions whose destination is on the next line. CommonMark allows one line ending there, so they still resolve to the same addresses.\n\n## Change requested: restore the Cloudflare platform names\n\nFollowing the child's condition \"no product names but GitHub\", the head makes these replacements:\n- \"Worker\" becomes \"worker\" throughout docs/usage-report.md, including the title;\n- \"Analytics Engine aggregate\" becomes \"analytics aggregate\";\n- \"Cloudflare account ID\" becomes \"provider account ID\";\n- the alternative note likewise uses \"worker\" 16 times and \"Worker\" none.\n\nThat condition is the plan 029 wording that Hugh corrected on 12 October (assert d250c7f9 on f384cab0): \"Public wording names GitHub, and